{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1538662909,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDEzNjkxOTE4OA=="},"target":"edc4bf98ff75112c944ee9dd7db71b83f6cc6b6fb18ff0c4574afb485f38b3a1","message":"#### What is the problem?\nApparently the recently added to annex ability to retry failed downloads is disabled ([annex.retry defaults to 0](http://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/some_transfers_for_get_-J4_fail_over_ssh__47__rsync_and_require_retry/#comment-cd8d46adf300f4b92a2caca6c6f5e803)) by default.  I first thought that we could just hardcode to provide e.g. `-c annex.retry=3` to all annex calls (`self._ANNEX_GIT_COMMON_OPTIONS`), but then thought that we better have a config setting for it defaulting to 3, BUT this is already git-annex'es config setting, which might be set and we would be forcefully overriding it.  So I wondered what should be our course of action?\n\nI think we could \n- define `datalad.annex.retry` common_cfg defaulting to 3 and describing that it would be used ONLY if configuration is not defining `annex.retry` config option\n- set it in `AnnexRepo.__init__` conditional as described above\n\nSounds like a reasonable plan or am I missing something?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1539705593,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMDI5NDkyMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2896#issuecomment-430294922"},"message":"your input @datalad/developers would be appreciated!","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1543723488,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDE5OTk3OTg3NzE="},"added":["on hold - input required"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1543723496,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0MzQ3OTU2OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/